<Base title="AI + Computation — Maheswaran" description="AI-enabled engineering, DOE, surrogate modelling, scientific ML, automation and engineering agents.">
  <section class="wrap">
    <div class="eyebrow">AI + Computation</div>
    <h1 style="font-size:52px;letter-spacing:-.04em;margin:10px 0 18px">From simulation data to faster engineering decisions.</h1>
    <p style="font-size:19px;line-height:1.7;color:#666;max-width:780px">This is the computation hub: data-driven CAE, scientific ML, optimization and automation. The emphasis is always on engineering usefulness, validation and knowing where a model stops being trustworthy.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section"><div class="wrap grid">
    <article id="ai-engineering" class="topic"><h3>AI for engineering</h3><ul><li>Data-driven CAE</li><li>Engineering copilots</li><li>RAG / knowledge workflows</li><li>Decision support</li><li>Physics-aware AI</li></ul></article>
    <article id="doe" class="topic"><h3>DOE & optimization</h3><ul><li>Design spaces</li><li>Sensitivity</li><li>Optimization loops</li><li>Multi-objective studies</li><li>Sampling strategy</li></ul></article>
    <article id="surrogates" class="topic"><h3>Surrogates & ROM</h3><ul><li>Regression surrogates</li><li>Reduced-order models</li><li>Extrapolation</li><li>Uncertainty</li><li>Validation</li></ul></article>
    <article id="scientific-ml" class="topic"><h3>Scientific ML</h3><ul><li>Physics-informed learning</li><li>Hybrid models</li><li>Operator learning</li><li>Simulation data</li><li>Generalization</li></ul></article>
  </div></section>

  <section id="automation" class="section"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="eyebrow">Automation & agents</div><h2>Engineering workflows that can act.</h2>
    <div class="card"><p style="margin:0;line-height:1.7">STAR-CCM+ automation, Python workflows, result extraction, model orchestration and future agentic CFD belong here. Individual tools or public demos can become dedicated subpages when they are substantial enough.</p></div>
  </div></section>
</Base>